🏎️ F1 Race Time Prediction Using Qualifying Performance
This project predicts Formula 1 race lap times using driver qualifying times. Leveraging machine learning and real-world data from the FastF1 API, it forecasts likely top finishers in an upcoming Grand Prix based on historical performance.

📂 Project Overview
Objective: Predict race pace from qualifying performance.
Target GP: 2025 Chinese Grand Prix
Data Sources:
  FastF1 for real 2024 race lap times
  Manually defined 2025 qualifying times
Model Used: Gradient Boosting Regressor (via sklearn)

⚙️ Technologies & Libraries
fastf1 – to access historical race data
pandas – for data manipulation
scikit-learn – for regression modeling and evaluation 
Python 3.10+

📊 Methodology
Data Collection:
   Lap times from the 2024 Chinese GP were pulled using FastF1.
   2025 Qualifying times were assumed and listed manually.
Data Mapping:
   Each driver was linked with their:
   Code (e.g., VER for Max Verstappen)
   Team (e.g., Red Bull)
   Country
Model Training:
   The Gradient Boosting Regressor was trained using:
   X: 2024 qualifying times
   y: 2024 actual race lap times
   Model performance was evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE).
Prediction:
   The model predicts race lap times for 2025 based on the qualifying input.
   Outputs include predicted lap time, country, team, and ranking with emojis 🥇🥈🥉.

📌 Example Output
