🎖️ Charles Leclerc Ferrari(MON) — Predicted Race Time: 90.899 s
🔍 Model MAE: 0.35 seconds

🧠 Insights
   Lower qualifying times usually indicate faster predicted race pace.
   Drivers from historically top-performing teams (e.g., Red Bull, Mercedes) rank higher.
   The model shows promising accuracy (low MAE).

🚀 How to Run
Install Dependencies:
   pip install fastf1 pandas scikit-learn
Run the Script:
    python chinese_gp_25.py
Make sure internet is enabled, as FastF1 pulls live F1 data.

📁 File Structure
   chinese_gp_25.py: Main script to fetch data, train the model, and display results.
   f1_cache/: Local FastF1 cache directory (auto-created).

📌 Future Improvements
  Add support for more seasons and dynamic qualifying inputs.
  Visualize results using matplotlib or plotly.
  Expand model to predict full race results (not just lap times).
  Include tire strategies or weather data for more accuracy.

